{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc",
    "description": "Gradient magnitude |grad u| of NCAR fire_behavior's fire_upwinding = 4 (classical Godunov discretization of the Hamiltonian; physics/level_set_mod.F90 Calc_tend_ls) on EarthSciDiscretizations' cartesian_uniform_2d grid with fire_behavior's own wall treatment. Calc_tend_ls tests `i < ids + BDY_ENO1 .or. i > ide - BDY_ENO1 .or. j < jds + BDY_ENO1 .or. j > jde - BDY_ENO1` BEFORE its `select case (fire_upwinding)`, so within bdy_eno1_cells (BDY_ENO1 = 10) of any wall grad = sqrt(Select_eno(difflx, diffrx)^2 + Select_eno(diffly, diffry)^2) for every scheme, case 4 included, with the wall cells' outer neighbour the guarded linear-extrapolation ghost of Extrapol_var_at_bdys; only away from the walls is grad the Rouy-Tourin Hamiltonian sqrt(max(D-x,0)^2 + min(D+x,0)^2 + max(D-y,0)^2 + min(D+y,0)^2). ESD's rules/godunov_norm_D2_dirichlet_bc applies the Hamiltonian everywhere and closes the walls with prescribed values, which is not what the reference does (with a zero wall value its wall |grad| is ~60 where fire_behavior's is ~1). COMPOUND MATCH (esm-spec 9.6.3): sqrt((D(u, wrt: x))^2 + (D(u, wrt: y))^2) at priority 20, scoped with where {u: {shape: [x, y]}}, the pattern and priority of ESD's other norm rules. BODY: sqrt(Gx^2 + Gy^2) with Gx, Gy ESD's per-axis boundary frames (rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame, rules/weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_frame: ENO1 strips and one-cell guarded linear-extrapolation ghosts, shared by every hybrid scheme of the family, valid for bdy_eno1_cells >= 3) around this file's interior stencils godunov_eno1_D1x_magnitude_interior / _D1y_, which on the frame's doubly-interior block take the ENO1 minmod (ESD stencils/eno1_minmod_D1x, _D1y) inside the wall band (ESD stencils/eno1_wall_band) and the per-axis Godunov magnitude sqrt(max(D-,0)^2 + min(D+,0)^2) elsewhere, so Gx^2 + Gy^2 is the ENO1 grad^2 in the band and the Rouy-Tourin Hamiltonian outside it. The per-axis quantity diff2x = max(D-,0) - min(D+,0) of the case-4 front normal is lowered by ESD's rules/godunov_upwind_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc, which already carry the same wall band and halo. Local to this repository because ESD has no Godunov norm rule with the ENO1 wall band. Free names (consumer scope): bdy_eno1_cells (>= 3), dx, dy. Requires NX, NY >= 7.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "discretization",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:norm_grad",
      "bc:extrapolate_linear",
      "fire_upwinding:4"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis, 29(3), 867-884.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls (case 4 and case 10, the `use eno1 near domain boundaries` band test that precedes the select case), Select_eno, Select_weno5, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. Identical in WRF phys/fire_behavior/physics/level_set_mod.F90."
      }
    ]
  },
